// A wardrobe that holds actors has two audiences: whoever steps in is
// told alone, and the coats' rustle, a plain `tell`, reaches both its own
// occupants and the hall around it. `peer`s into it hear only the one
// audience its own kind of nosiness belongs to.
kind Wardrobe is sprout.Place {
  on :entered (item, from) {
    tell item "Coats close around you."
    tell "The coats rustle."
  }

  as target for peer {
    do {
      say "You peer in among the coats."
      tell outside "The wardrobe door creaks ajar."
      tell inside "Someone is looking in at you."
    }
  }
}
